System & Role
You are an expert Front-End Web Developer and UI/UX Designer specializing in modern WebGL animations, Tailwind CSS, and React/Next.js.
Objective
Build a modern, interactive landing page for PHYSICHEM—a high-end coaching institute specializing in Physics and Chemistry for classes 9th through 12th. Use the attached video as the visual, structural, and motion reference for the website layout.
Brand & Design Directives
Brand Name: PHYSICHEM
Target Audience: Students in grades 9, 10, 11, and 12, plus parents looking for premier science coaching.
Aesthetic Style: Neumorphic-Glassmorphic dark/light hybrid canvas with smooth viewport transitions, HUD-style framing, and high-tech dynamic 3D visual assets (referencing the frame aesthetic from the video).
Color Palette: Matte gray canvas (#E5E5E5 or dark tech equivalent), glowing neon accents (representing physical energy & chemical reactions), dark slate typography, and glassmorphic card overlays.
Page Sections & Motion Flow (Based on Video Reference)
Section 1: Hero
Headline: "Master Physics & Chemistry from Class 9 to 12"
Subheadline: "Building strong conceptual foundations and target-driven results for board exams, JEE, and NEET."
CTAs: Pill button ENROLL NOW + Outline button EXPLORE COURSES.
Visual: Central animated WebGL dynamic sphere/particle system (symbolizing atomic structures and energy fields).
Section 2: Agency / Mission Statement
Headline: "WE ARE A RESULT-ORIENTED SCIENCE ACADEMY."
Content: Focused on conceptual clarity, interactive learning, and continuous assessment.
Animation: Camera transition/zoom on the central 3D element with typography cross-fade.
Section 3: Class Offerings (Services Grid)
Headline: "DISCOVER OUR PROGRAMS"
Cards (Staggered Scroll Entrance):
Foundation (Classes 9 & 10): Focus on building core concepts in physics and chemistry early.
Senior Secondary (Classes 11 & 12): Comprehensive coverage of Board syllabus + competitive exam preparation.
Test Series & Doubt Solving: Dedicated regular testing, personalized mentorship, and one-on-one doubt clearing.
Card Icons: 3D glassmorphic geometric shapes (e.g., atom model, prism/molecule, diamond crystal lattice).
Tech Stack & Architecture Requirements
Framework: React / Next.js (App Router)
Styling: Tailwind CSS + Framer Motion (or GSAP ScrollTrigger for section pinning)
3D Visuals: Three.js / React Three Fiber / Lucide Icons
Persistent HUD UI: Top navigation bar (HOME, COURSES, FACULTY, RESULTS, CONTACT), fixed section counter (001 / 005), bottom scroll mouse indicator, and share action button.
Instructions
Analyze the attached video for layout structure, card entrance timings, and background transitions.
Generate clean, modular, and fully responsive code using React and Tailwind CSS.
Include inline CSS keyframes or Framer Motion variant objects for all micro-interactions and scroll-triggered section steps.